course: dictionary
lesson: 5604
title: Lifeless: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one the writer means. Lifeless is one of these words. «The Atacama Desert in Chile is the driest non-polar desert, and its soil is so dry and lifeless, much like Mars.» The clues dry and Mars tell you lifeless means having no living things.
explain: Lifeless can mean dead, or never having had life. A stone has never been alive, so it is lifeless in that second sense. Read the sentence, then ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: Lifeless can also describe a voice, a story or a performance with no energy or excitement. A lifeless story is dull, not dead. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Lifeless means dead, or never having had life.
fact: Lifeless can describe a place with no living things, like a lifeless planet.
fact: Lifeless can also mean dull, without energy or excitement.
fact: «The soil is so dry and lifeless, much like Mars, that scientists test Mars rovers there.»
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The Atacama soil is so dry and lifeless, much like Mars.» What does lifeless mean here? | Full of energy and noise | Lively and bright | *With no living things | Very wet and muddy
exercise: Your teacher says Ben's story is lifeless. What does she probably mean? | *Dull, with no energy or excitement | Written in a new language | Full of living animals | Very frightening and loud
exercise: Scientists say the Moon is lifeless. What does this mean? | A busy city with lots of people | It is always raining | *It has no living things | It is full of music
test: «Her voice was lifeless, so the class stopped listening.» What does lifeless suggest? | Happy and singing | Fast and excited | Loud and cheerful | *Dull, with no energy
test: «The lifeless rock had been there for a million years.» What does lifeless mean here? | Sleepy and tired | *Never having had life | Freshly painted | Full of insects
exam: What is the best meaning of lifeless in «The lifeless planet had no plants or animals»? | Covered in snow | Very large and bright | Full of people | *Having no living things
